  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In the adjoining figure, \\(PQ\\) is a diagonal of the cube. If \\(PQ\\) has length \\(a,\\) then the surface area of the cube is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2a^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(2\\sqrt2a^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(2\\sqrt3a^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3\\sqrt3a^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(6a^2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1981-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If the side length is \\(s,\\) then the space diagonal is \\(s\\sqrt3=a,\\) so \\(s^2=\\frac{a^2}{3}.\\) The surface area is \\(6s^2=6(\\frac{a^2}{3})=2a^2.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Relate the cube’s space diagonal to its side length",
        "Substitute the side length into the formula for six square faces"
      ],
